keywords:
  - egocentric video
  - optical flow
  - hand speed
  - background capture
  - hand activity level
  - occupational ergonomics
abstract: >-
  Box-median dense optical flow inside a detected hand box under egocentric camera motion
  silently switches from tracking the hand to tracking the background, settling on the scene
  depth ratio across Farneback, DIS, RAFT-small, and RAFT-large with zero null fields.
  Direct pixel-level inspection, a static-camera moving-hand control, and controlled sweeps
  over depth ratio, box size, motion blur, sensor noise, and decode resolution isolate the
  mechanism and its downstream impact on hand-activity estimation.
